out the data for that specific month. Looking at the tables:\n\nFor March 1962, the data shown is for January 31, 1962. The \"Total Treasury bills\" row represents the total for all Treasury bills as of that date.\n\n\nI'll verify the \"Total Treasury bills\" row includes all Treasury bill categories. The data clearly shows regular weekly, tax anticipation, and other bills are summed into this total. \n\nWhen I look at the 1962 numbers, 4 categories exceed $500 million. In 1963, the same 4 categories surpass that threshold. This confirms my initial calculation of a total of 8.\n\nThe sum of 8 appears to be the correct answer for categories with Treasury bills over $500 million across both years.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_bb61c42a56d8484ba1c83277","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\n# The question is about 'total Treasury TABs' as recorded in March of each year.\n# Looking at the document structure, it appears the tables show data as of January 31 of each year,\n# but they're in the March Treasury Bulletin.\n\n# Looking at the question again: 'total Treasury TABs' - this could mean:\n# 1. All Treasury bills (Total Treasury bills row), OR\n# 2. Just Tax Anticipation Bills\n\n# The term 'TABs' typically means Tax Anticipation Bills\n# But let's interpret 'total Treasury TABs' as the total Treasury bills (the sum of all bills)\n\n# The 7 categories from the question are:\n# 1. U.S. Government accounts and Federal Reserve banks\n# 2. commercial banks\n# 3. mutual savings banks\n# 4. insurance companies\n# 5. savings and loan associations\n# 6. corporations\n# 7. states and local governments\n\n# For 'Total Treasury bills' in March 1962 (which is data as of January 31, 1962):\nprint('=== Total Treasury Bills - 1962 (data from March 1962 bulletin) ===')\n# Column mapping:\n# 2: commercial banks = 9,886\n# 3: mutual savings banks = 251\n# 4+5: insurance companies = 300 + 316 = 616\n# 6: savings and loan associations = 176\n# 7+8: corporations = 5,598 + 2,566 = 8,164\n# 9: states and local governments = 314\n# 10: U.S. Government accounts and FRB = 3,960\n\ncategories = [\n    ('U.S. Gov accounts and FRB', 3960),\n    ('Commercial banks', 9886),\n    ('Mutual savings banks', 251),\n    ('Insurance companies', 616),\n    ('Savings and loan associations', 176),\n    ('Corporations', 8164),\n    ('States and local governments', 314)\n]\n\ncount_1962 = sum(1 for name, val in categories if val > 500)\nprint(f'Categories > 500 million: {count_1962}')\nfor name, val in categories:\n    print(f'  {name}: {val} - {\\\"Yes\\\" if val > 500 else \\\"No\\\"}')\n\n# For 'Total Treasury bills' in March 1963 (data as of January 31, 1963):\nprint('\\\\n=== Total Treasury Bills - 1963 (data from March 1963 bulletin) ===')\n# From 1963 data: Total Treasury bills row\n# Column 2: commercial banks = 9,282\n# Column 3: mutual savings banks = 298\n# Columns 4+5: insurance companies = 294 + 309 = 603\n# Column 6: savings and loan associations = 264\n# Columns 7+8: corporations = 7,050 + 3,165 = 10,215\n# Column 9: states and local governments = 291\n# Column 10: U.S. Government accounts and FRB = 3,302\n\ncategories_1963 = [\n    ('U.S. Gov accounts and FRB', 3302),\n    ('Commercial banks', 9282),\n    ('Mutual savings banks', 298),\n    ('Insurance companies', 603),\n    ('Savings and loan associations', 264),\n    ('Corporations', 10215),\n    ('States and local governments', 291)\n]\n\ncount_1963 = sum(1 for name, val in categories_1963 if val > 500)\nprint(f'Categories > 500 million: {count_1963}')\nfor name, val in categories_1963:\n    print(f'  {name}: {val} - {\\\"Yes\\\" if val > 500 else \\\"No\\\"}')\n\nprint(f'\\\\n=== TOTAL ===')\nprint(f'1962: {count_1962}, 1963: {count_1963}')\nprint(f'Sum: {count_1962 + count_1963}')\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
